The second item is the open twin of the first closed item
(\cref{app:knowledge-items}): a line of plain English typed at the
prompt, and the question what happens.
In the start quiz it is the only form the question takes, since the
closed alternatives---\enquote{the shell looks for a program called
show}---would hand a student who has never met a shell the very model
the module is about to teach; the account written here is the starting
point against which the closed item at the end is read.

