Textual feedback is the system's response, and an error message is
information, not failure (\cref{sec:shell}).
The item shows a command that produced a message and asks what the
message means.
The correct answer reads the message as reporting that the action did
not happen; the distractors dismiss it as an ignorable warning, blame the
terminal, or take one message to mean the shell itself has stopped.

