\subsubsection{The remote shell}

Files live on machines: a file created on the remote host is on that
host, not on the laptop (\cref{sec:ssh}).
The item runs a program over SSH that writes a file, closes the
connection, and asks where the file is.
The correct answer keeps the file on the server where the program ran;
the distractors bring it home to the laptop, sync it to both, or treat it
as vanishing with the connection.
It opens the remote-shell items: a concrete round trip whose answer
shows at once whether files live on machines for the student, before
the two items that follow ask where the shell itself is.

