The interface is invariant while the machine varies (\cref{sec:ssh}):
a chained [[ssh]] nests one shell inside another, and [[exit]] peels off
the innermost.
The item nests two sessions and asks where a single [[exit]] leaves the
student; it is the discernment behind the ssh-cycle that our course
observations report---students who chain [[ssh]] onward and back have
not discerned that each session is one machine and that leaving one
returns to the one below.
The correct answer steps back one machine; the distractors collapse the
whole chain, treat [[exit]] as cosmetic, or close the terminal.
(An earlier version asked for the \emph{best way} to switch between
machines, which measured a preferred practice rather than a discerned
aspect.)

